From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 04:18:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 143/225] ASoC: sprd: port the AP-side i2s0 audio path from the
 5.4 vendor tree

Extend the vendor audio port beyond the working VBC/agcp card (hw:0,0)
to the AP-side i2s0 path. Ports two drivers from the 5.4 out-of-tree
audio_driver into sound/soc/sprd/vendor/:

  - sprd-i2s.c            (unisoc,i2s CPU-DAI, was dai/i2s/i2s.c)
  - sprd-i2s-null-codec.c (unisoc,i2s-null-codec "all-i2s" card)
  - i2s.h                 (config defines)

All platform glue it needs already exists in the ported tree: the
sprd-dmaengine-pcm platform binds unisoc,sharkl5-pcm-platform and
already calls sprd_i2s_dai_to_config() for the i2s DMA use-cases, and
the arch_audio_i2s_* / ap_apb_gpr helpers are implemented inline in
sprd-audio-agcp.h / sprd-asoc-common.c. Defining CONFIG_SND_SOC_UNISOC_I2S
in the bundle Makefile flips sprd-i2s.h to export the real symbols.

Only 6.x API delta needed: platform_driver.remove now returns void.

DT: add the ap_dma controller (0x20000000, GIC_SPI 24) -- absent from
the mainline ums512.dtsi since upstream audio only uses agcp_dma -- plus
the i2s0 controller (0x70c00000) and the sprd-pcm-iis + all-i2s card
nodes. The board dts enables the path in stock PCM/BT-SCO config.

Unlike the VBC path, i2s0 rides the AP-owned ap_dma, so its DMA
completion IRQ (GIC_SPI 24) is a normal AP interrupt and should deliver
period wakeups natively -- no hrtimer workaround expected. Untested on
hardware; the 2-stage-usecase interrupt-source routing still needs
on-device verification.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
